      "type": "General Statements: All Other Content",
      "notes": "Magnesium is an essential electrolyte mineral involved in maintaining proper cardiovascular, nerve, and muscle health. The primary function is to activate enzymes. More than half of the body's magnesium is stored in the bones, 27% in muscle and the remainder in soft body tissues, cells and fluids. Magnesium is critical in energy production."
